{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.53.12.144","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1426474070,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":2,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"4dde30a1b76da266f039802948a362e9","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Honestly, &amp;nbsp;a lot brides get married legally at home just before or after their destination wedding. My fianc\u00e9 and I will be having a symbolic ceremony in Mexico. It will save you a big headache from what i&#039;ve heard. It&#039;s all a matter of personal preference and in the beginning it was difficult for me to decide because I wanted to be legally married while I was in Mexico.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889361,"PostDate":1426473892,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Honestly, \u00a0a lot brides get married legally at home just before or after their destination wedding. My fianc\u00e9 and I will be having a symbolic ceremony in Mexico. It will save you a big headache from what i've heard. It's all a matter of personal preference and in the beginning it was difficult for me to decide because I wanted to be legally married while I was in Mexico.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div><br><div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<p><span style=\"color:#808080;\"><span style=\"font-size:14px;\">My planning thread :<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78755-perianjay-planning-thread-december-15-2015-beach-palace\/#entry1885631<\/a>","Email":"perianjohnson@gmail.com","IpAddress":"66.241.131.23","GroupId":3,"GroupName":"Member","JoinDate":1419437814,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-281478.jpg?_r=1428347017","PhotoWidth":169,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"perianjay","Id":281478,"Name":"perianjay","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"216.23.195.134","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"34df53e9474b4cf1d880f9265dce1148","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;It&#039;s definitely a personal preference. I have heard one of the other and usually the resorts are very accommodating to your needs. I know it can be a headache on getting every document translated, the&amp;nbsp;apostille and the blood test. We decided to do a symbolic ceremony instead. We have an officiant who will marry us at home two days before we arrive into Mexico. I have notified our guests that we will be doing an the exchange of our rings.&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1889386,"PostDate":1426510074,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>It's definitely a personal preference. I have heard one of the other and usually the resorts are very accommodating to your needs. I know it can be a headache on getting every document translated, the\u00a0apostille and the blood test. We decided to do a symbolic ceremony instead. We have an officiant who will marry us at home two days before we arrive into Mexico. I have notified our guests that we will be doing an the exchange of our rings.<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p><strong>N&C<\/strong><\/p>\n<p><em>April 17, 2015<\/em><\/p>\n<p>Gran Caribe Real (Cancun, Mexico)<\/p>\n<p>Including Bride & Groom: 22 guests (19 adults & 3 children)","Email":"nancysoup@att.net","IpAddress":"216.23.195.134","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1411661062,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-280004.jpg?_r=1412891058","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"hellosassypants","Id":280004,"Name":"hellosassypants","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"149.254.181.226","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78709,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"1cf18f5b2cbbcaa67b542440e756cb76","RawContent":"[quote name=\"perianjay\" post=\"1889361\" timestamp=\"1426473892\"]\nHonestly,  a lot brides get married legally at home just before or after their destination wedding. My fianc\u00e9 and I will be having a symbolic ceremony in Mexico. It will save you a big headache from what i&#039;ve heard. It&#039;s all a matter of personal preference and in the beginning it was difficult for me to decide because I wanted to be legally married while I was in Mexico.[\/quote]We have now decided to do the same.  Too much hassle getting certificate back to UK some say 3 weeks others say 3-6 months  xx\n\nMaybeoneday\n14 October 2015....waiting confirmation\nRoyalton Riviera Cancun, Mexico","Attachments":[],"Id":1889952,"PostDate":1426751597,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p class='citation' style='color:#324F85;margin:15px;font-weight:bold;font-style:italic;'>perianjay, on 15 March 2015 - 06:44 PM, said:<\/p><div class='blockquote'><div class='quote'><p>Honestly,  a lot brides get married legally at home just before or after their destination wedding. My fianc\u00e9 and I will be having a symbolic ceremony in Mexico. It will save you a big headache from what i've heard. It's all a matter of personal preference and in the beginning it was difficult for me to decide because I wanted to be legally married while I was in Mexico.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\nWe have now decided to do the same.  Too much hassle getting certificate back to UK some say 3 weeks others say 3-6 months  xx<br><br>\nMaybeoneday<br>\n14 October 2015....waiting confirmation<br>\nRoyalton Riviera Cancun, Mexico\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"shelina_nessa@yahoo.co.uk","IpAddress":"149.254.56.238","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1421821539,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":false,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_images\/destination\/profile\/default_large.png","PhotoWidth":125,"PhotoHeight":125,"PhotoType":""},"FormattedName":"maybeoneday","Id":281816,"Name":"maybeoneday","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":13,"TotalPages":2,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":10},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
